WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.811
Welcome to Nabulines Academy.

2
00:00:02.276 --> 00:00:03.796
In this lesson, we're going to show you

3
00:00:03.866 --> 00:00:06.130
exactly how this academy is structured —

4
00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:08.696
how lessons, exercises, and projects fit

5
00:00:08.731 --> 00:00:11.180
together — so you can learn as fast as

6
00:00:11.238 --> 00:00:13.270
possible and actually build real things.

7
00:00:13.909 --> 00:00:14.954
Let's get into it.

8
00:00:14.954 --> 00:00:17.067
First, let's talk about the structure.

9
00:00:17.473 --> 00:00:19.644
This academy is organized into chapters.

10
00:00:20.283 --> 00:00:22.222
Each chapter covers one major skill or

11
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:22.686
tool.

12
00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:25.693
Inside each chapter, you'll find lessons —

13
00:00:25.914 --> 00:00:27.620
short, focused videos like this one.

14
00:00:28.259 --> 00:00:30.140
Every lesson teaches you one specific

15
00:00:30.186 --> 00:00:30.511
thing.

16
00:00:31.057 --> 00:00:31.823
One concept.

17
00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:32.636
One tool.

18
00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:33.437
One step.

19
00:00:34.076 --> 00:00:35.655
We keep them short and clear so you can

20
00:00:35.689 --> 00:00:37.477
actually finish them and move forward.

21
00:00:37.477 --> 00:00:39.102
Every lesson has three parts.

22
00:00:39.648 --> 00:00:41.587
First, the video — that's what you're

23
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:42.504
watching right now.

24
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.209
We explain the concept, show you real

25
00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:47.554
examples on screen, and walk through every

26
00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:48.042
step.

27
00:00:48.913 --> 00:00:51.746
Second, a quiz — a few quick questions to

28
00:00:51.804 --> 00:00:53.836
check that you understood the core ideas.

29
00:00:54.706 --> 00:00:57.655
And third, an exercise — a small task you

30
00:00:57.737 --> 00:00:59.420
actually do yourself to practice what you

31
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.163
just learned.

32
00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.346
The exercise is where the real learning

33
00:01:02.404 --> 00:01:03.112
happens.

34
00:01:03.112 --> 00:01:05.782
Here's the key: don't skip the exercises.

35
00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:08.778
Watching videos feels like learning, but

36
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:09.730
it's not enough.

37
00:01:10.275 --> 00:01:12.040
You have to type the commands, click the

38
00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:14.083
buttons, and see the results yourself.

39
00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:15.628
That's when it clicks.

40
00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:18.019
That's when you actually remember it.

41
00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:20.016
If you only watch, you'll forget

42
00:01:20.062 --> 00:01:20.887
everything in a week.

43
00:01:21.177 --> 00:01:22.976
If you do the exercises, you'll build real

44
00:01:23.035 --> 00:01:24.056
skills that stick.

45
00:01:24.056 --> 00:01:25.635
At the end of most chapters, there's a

46
00:01:25.693 --> 00:01:26.250
project.

47
00:01:26.796 --> 00:01:28.839
A project is bigger than an exercise —

48
00:01:29.246 --> 00:01:30.604
it's where you combine everything you

49
00:01:30.662 --> 00:01:31.928
learned in that chapter and build

50
00:01:31.986 --> 00:01:32.752
something real.

51
00:01:33.158 --> 00:01:34.017
Your first site.

52
00:01:34.308 --> 00:01:35.144
Your first app.

53
00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:37.593
Your first deployed page on the internet.

54
00:01:38.336 --> 00:01:40.101
Projects are your proof that you can

55
00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:41.076
actually do this.

56
00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:43.271
They're also what you'll show people when

57
00:01:43.305 --> 00:01:44.954
you say, I built this.

58
00:01:44.954 --> 00:01:46.893
Now let's talk about how to learn fast.

59
00:01:47.241 --> 00:01:49.679
The secret is consistency, not cramming.

60
00:01:50.225 --> 00:01:52.001
You don't need to spend eight hours a day

61
00:01:52.059 --> 00:01:52.582
on this.

62
00:01:53.127 --> 00:01:54.428
You need to spend a little bit of time

63
00:01:54.474 --> 00:01:55.101
regularly.

64
00:01:55.322 --> 00:01:57.400
Thirty minutes a day, five days a week —

65
00:01:57.748 --> 00:01:59.316
that's better than binging for six hours

66
00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.394
once and then disappearing for two weeks.

67
00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.751
Your brain needs repetition and time to

68
00:02:03.809 --> 00:02:04.935
absorb new ideas.

69
00:02:05.341 --> 00:02:07.373
Show up regularly, even if it's just for

70
00:02:07.431 --> 00:02:08.313
half an hour.

71
00:02:08.313 --> 00:02:09.915
Here's a simple schedule that works.

72
00:02:10.461 --> 00:02:12.051
Pick three to five days a week.

73
00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.768
On each of those days, watch one or two

74
00:02:14.838 --> 00:02:17.171
lessons, do the quizzes, and complete the

75
00:02:17.229 --> 00:02:17.996
exercises.

76
00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:19.215
That's it.

77
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.479
If you do that, you'll finish a chapter

78
00:02:21.548 --> 00:02:22.454
every week or two.

79
00:02:23.093 --> 00:02:25.206
If you skip the exercises and just watch,

80
00:02:25.461 --> 00:02:27.574
you'll finish faster — but you won't

81
00:02:27.609 --> 00:02:28.642
actually learn anything.

82
00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.487
Speed without doing is just wasted time.

83
00:02:31.487 --> 00:02:33.739
When you get stuck — and you will get

84
00:02:33.797 --> 00:02:36.363
stuck, everyone does — don't just give up

85
00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:37.141
and move on.

86
00:02:38.151 --> 00:02:38.708
Pause.

87
00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:41.704
Re-watch the part you didn't understand.

88
00:02:42.249 --> 00:02:43.399
Try the step again.

89
00:02:44.037 --> 00:02:45.349
Google the error message.

90
00:02:45.988 --> 00:02:46.801
Ask Claude.

91
00:02:47.671 --> 00:02:50.004
Most problems have simple fixes, but you

92
00:02:50.063 --> 00:02:51.467
have to actually try to solve them.

93
00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.161
Getting unstuck is a skill, and you get

94
00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.960
better at it every time you practice.

95
00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.969
One more thing: this academy assumes

96
00:02:58.027 --> 00:02:59.257
you're starting from zero.

97
00:02:59.896 --> 00:03:01.881
We define every technical word the first

98
00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:02.729
time it appears.

99
00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.178
We show every click and every command.

100
00:03:05.921 --> 00:03:07.907
If something feels too basic, that's by

101
00:03:07.965 --> 00:03:10.263
design — we're making sure no one gets

102
00:03:10.321 --> 00:03:11.018
left behind.

103
00:03:11.888 --> 00:03:14.141
If something feels too fast, slow down.

104
00:03:14.779 --> 00:03:15.638
Pause the video.

105
00:03:16.382 --> 00:03:17.067
Rewind.

106
00:03:17.705 --> 00:03:18.785
Go at your own pace.

107
00:03:19.075 --> 00:03:20.991
There's no timer and no one judging you.

108
00:03:20.991 --> 00:03:22.558
Finally, remember the goal.

109
00:03:22.965 --> 00:03:24.637
You're not here to collect certificates or

110
00:03:24.695 --> 00:03:25.867
watch a hundred videos.

111
00:03:26.215 --> 00:03:27.632
You're here to build real things and

112
00:03:27.678 --> 00:03:29.362
become someone who can actually create

113
00:03:29.385 --> 00:03:30.012
with code.

114
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.845
Every lesson, every exercise, every

115
00:03:32.903 --> 00:03:35.050
project — they all point toward that.

116
00:03:35.596 --> 00:03:36.908
By the end of this path, you'll have

117
00:03:36.943 --> 00:03:39.485
deployed sites, built apps, and automated

118
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:40.101
tasks.

119
00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:42.527
You'll have a portfolio of real work.

120
00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:43.978
That's what matters.

121
00:03:43.978 --> 00:03:46.172
Alright, that's how this academy works.

122
00:03:46.915 --> 00:03:48.959
Your exercise for this lesson is simple:

123
00:03:49.597 --> 00:03:50.398
set a schedule.

124
00:03:51.037 --> 00:03:52.674
Pick which days of the week you'll learn,

125
00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.125
and how long you'll spend.

126
00:03:55.135 --> 00:03:56.795
Write it down or set a reminder on your

127
00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:57.202
phone.

128
00:03:57.945 --> 00:03:59.756
Consistency is everything.

129
00:04:00.766 --> 00:04:02.763
Next lesson, we're diving into what AI

130
00:04:02.821 --> 00:04:04.504
really is and why it changes everything

131
00:04:04.562 --> 00:04:05.247
for beginners.

132
00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:06.362
See you there.
